executionContract.intendedBehavior:
All six transfer modes (materialize, export, verify, agents, toolchain, dependencies) spawn only through openGuestStream. openGuestStream:
- validates its inputs;
- reads the guest's address fresh from multipass info ipv4[0] (strict dotted quad);
- spawns the pinned OpenSSH client (provider.ssh ?? sshExecutable(process.platform)) with exactly sshStreamArgv({...transportFiles(name, keyDir), name, address, mode}) and PIPES.
It refuses before any spawn with TRANSPORT_INPUT_INVALID or TRANSPORT_ADDRESS_UNKNOWN. Transfers map a transport refusal or spawn failure to TRANSFER_SPAWN_FAILED, and any non-zero exit (ssh's 255 included) to TRANSFER_EXIT_FAILED. A stall still ends in TRANSFER_TIMEOUT with SIGKILL. readGuestInfo additionally returns address.
